{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ecs"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted"]},{"title":"Modules","anchor":"Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Build games and simulations from entities, the components they hold, and systems that update","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them in a declared order.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ECS is an entity component system for Swift. It suits any program that updates many similar"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"things each step, such as the bodies of a physics simulation or the characters of a game."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entities are lightweight handles. An "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity"},{"type":"text","text":" holds no data of its own."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Components are plain value types, such as a position or a velocity, attached to entities."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","type":"reference"},{"text":" holds the entities and their components, along with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"resources"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values the world holds once, such as a clock.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems are rules that read and change the world through queries and updates, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs them in the order you write, at the same time where they don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conflict."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" runs a world frame by frame, with a fixed timestep and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"states.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world is a copy-on-write value, like an array: copies are cheap and independent, so you can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keep one for a snapshot, an undo step or a rollback."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example, using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" components from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", spawns a ball and moves it one step by its velocity:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import ECS","","var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","    position.y += row.components.dy","}","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"import ECS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation, and you can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"import one on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","title":"ECS","role":"collection","externalID":"ECS","modules":[{"name":"ECS"}]},"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","title":"World","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A collection of entities, the components they hold, and resources.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://ECS/documentation/ECS":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Build games and simulations from entities, the components they hold, and systems that update","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them in a declared order.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ecs","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS","title":"ECS"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Entity":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity","title":"Entity","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle that identifies one entity in a world."}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/entity","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://ECS/documentation/ECS/GettingStarted":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Define components, spawn entities, and move them with systems that run in a schedule and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simulation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ecs\/gettingstarted","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted","title":"Getting Started with ECS"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","title":"WorldModule","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Store the state of a game or simulation as entities and components, and read and change it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"queries, updates, and commands.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Simulation","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Simulation","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A world and its schedules by label, advanced one frame at a time."}],"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","title":"Simulation"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","title":"Schedule","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","title":"Systems","role":"collection